{
    "background_story": "Nico grew up in a low-income neighborhood where voting rights were often suppressed. Despite the obstacles, he was determined to make his voice heard. As a young adult, Nico became involved in local activism, fighting for the rights of marginalized communities. However, he soon realized that the system was stacked against them. Polling stations were scarce, voter ID laws were restrictive, and gerrymandering was rampant. Nico's own family had been disenfranchised for generations, their votes diluted by unfair districting. He decided to take action, organizing voter registration drives and advocating for electoral reform. Nico's efforts were met with resistance, but he refused to back down. He continued to fight for the rights of his community, inspiring others to join him in the struggle for a fair and equal democracy.",
